From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 119/159] Input: Add Awinic AW8695 haptics driver

The AW8695 is an I2C driver for linear resonant actuators (LRA), found
in Motorola phones such as the Moto G 5G Plus.

Add a force-feedback driver for it. FF_RUMBLE effects are played in
the chip's continuous (CONT) mode, which drives the LRA at its
resonant frequency and tracks it through zero-crossing detection; the
strong magnitude sets the drive level. The f0, drive and overdrive
levels, brake cycles, drive time and zero-crossing threshold come from
the device tree, as tuned per device by the vendor (awinic,*
properties). The chip is held in reset by an optional GPIO until
probe.

The RAM waveform library, the vendor sysfs interface and the f0
calibration of the downstream driver are not implemented.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
